{
 "tickets": [
  {
   "body": "Hello support, I am trying to figure out how we can adjust our portal settings so that patients don't see sensitive diagnostic results immediately. We want to set up a delayed release timer, maybe a 48 or 72-hour hold, especially for things like pathology or imaging reports, so our provider has a chance to review them with the patient first. I looked under the settings tab and found the patient portal section, but I couldn't see any obvious options for automated delays. Could you point me in the right direction or let me know if this requires changing global rules?",
   "id": "gen-141",
   "subject": "Question about setting up delayed release for patient portal results"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hi there, I need assistance checking the state prescription monitoring program database through the software, as we keep hitting an access error when querying patient fill histories. Please let me know how to resolve this.",
   "id": "gen-142",
   "subject": "Medication history database access error"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, I am so sorry to bother you, but our entire office is completely dead in the water right now regarding pharmacy searches. Every time we try to look up a local pharmacy or update a patient's preferred location, the system spins indefinitely or throws a blank error screen. We have patients waiting in the lobby and we can't send any new electronic prescriptions out. Is there a widespread outage happening right now, and when can we expect it to be fixed?",
   "id": "gen-143",
   "subject": "Apologies, but pharmacy directory is completely down for us"
  },
  {
   "body": "Our lab feed from Quest has stopped populating as of this morning. Please check the interface connection.",
   "id": "gen-144",
   "subject": "Missing lab feed connection"
  },
  {
   "body": "Dear Support Team, We are writing to inquire about the standard workflow for routing abnormal diagnostic results to covering physicians while our primary providers are out of office. Specifically, we would like to know if there is an automated delegation feature or if this must be handled manually on a case-by-case basis within the lab review queue. Thank you for your guidance on this matter.",
   "id": "gen-145",
   "subject": "Inquiry Regarding Routing Lab Results to Covering Physicians"
  },
  {
   "body": "I've been trying to update a patient's preferred pharmacy for the last twenty minutes because their usual spot permanently closed down, but the directory search is totally useless. It won't find the new location by zip code, and when I tried to look up how to put a custom pharmacy in manually, the help guide didn't make any sense. This is really slowing down our check-in desk. Can someone please tell me how we are actually supposed to add a custom pharmacy entry when it's not showing up in the main database?",
   "id": "gen-146",
   "subject": "Can't update closed pharmacy or add custom ones"
  },
  {
   "body": "We need to update a patient's preferred pharmacy location, but the search tool isn't bringing up the new branch. How do we add a custom pharmacy entry into the system?",
   "id": "gen-147",
   "subject": "Updating and adding pharmacy entries"
  },
  {
   "body": "Can you tell me how to forward abnormal lab results over to a covering doctor? The current setup is confusing and I need it handled quickly.",
   "id": "gen-148",
   "subject": "Routing labs to covering physicians"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hi team, I am looking at our denial management tools and I am a bit lost. We are trying to figure out how to pull reports on specific denial reason codes so we can address recurring billing issues with a few major payers, but the reporting dashboard has so many filters that I'm not sure which ones apply to appeals. Also, when we attach clinical notes to a denied claim, is there a way to make sure it links directly to the appeal form? Any screenshots or simple steps would be great.",
   "id": "gen-149",
   "subject": "Help with tracking insurance claim denials and pulling reports"
  },
  {
   "body": "How do we route abnormal lab results to a covering provider when the primary doctor is out? Please provide instructions.",
   "id": "gen-150",
   "subject": "Routing abnormal lab results"
  }
 ]
}
